<!-- ========== SETUP GUIDE ========== -->
<section class="section" id="setup">
  <div class="sec-title">30-Day <span>Setup</span> Roadmap</div>
  <div class="sec-sub">// HOW TO IMPLEMENT THIS FRAMEWORK AT TRANE TECHNOLOGIES</div>

  <div class="setup-steps">

    <div class="setup-step">
      <div class="step-num">1</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Week 1 — Install Testsigma + Connect Jira</h3>
        <p>Start with Testsigma as your AI testing hub. Connect it to your existing Jira workspace so requirements flow in and defects flow out automatically.</p>
        <div class="code-block">
<span class="comment"># Step 1: Sign up at testsigma.com (cloud, no install)</span>
<span class="comment"># Step 2: Connect Jira integration</span>
Settings → Integrations → Jira → Enter Jira URL + API token
<span class="comment"># Step 3: Import your first user story</span>
Test Cases → Import from Jira → Select sprint backlog
<span class="comment"># Step 4: Let AI generate test cases</span>
Click "Generate with AI" → Review → Approve → Done
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
      <div class="step-num">2</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Week 1-2 — Add Healenium to Existing Selenium</h3>
        <p>If you already have a Selenium suite, add Healenium in 15 minutes. Your existing tests immediately get AI self-healing — no rewrite needed.</p>
        <div class="code-block">
<span class="comment"># Maven pom.xml — add this dependency:</span>
&lt;<span class="kw">dependency</span>&gt;
  &lt;<span class="kw">groupId</span>&gt;com.epam.healenium&lt;/<span class="kw">groupId</span>&gt;
  &lt;<span class="kw">artifactId</span>&gt;healenium-web&lt;/<span class="kw">artifactId</span>&gt;
  &lt;<span class="kw">version</span>&gt;3.4.2&lt;/<span class="kw">version</span>&gt;
&lt;/<span class="kw">dependency</span>&gt;

<span class="comment"># In your test setup — wrap your driver:</span>
<span class="kw">WebDriver</span> driver = <span class="kw">new</span> ChromeDriver();
<span class="kw">SelfHealingDriver</span> healingDriver = SelfHealingDriver.create(driver);
<span class="comment"># That's it — Healenium now auto-fixes broken locators</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
      <div class="step-num">3</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Week 2 — Set Up AI Prompting Workflow for Test Cases</h3>
        <p>Train your QA team to use Claude or ChatGPT effectively for test case generation. Create reusable prompt templates for Trane-specific testing.</p>
        <div class="code-block">
<span class="comment">## TRANE TEAM PROMPT TEMPLATE — Test Case Generation:</span>

You are a Senior QA Engineer for Trane Technologies (HVAC systems).
Write detailed test cases for the following user story:

<span class="str">[PASTE USER STORY HERE]</span>

Include:
- Positive test cases (happy path)
- Negative test cases (invalid inputs, edge cases)
- Boundary value analysis
- Preconditions and test data
- Expected results in measurable terms
Format as: Test Case ID | Title | Steps | Expected Result
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
      <div class="step-num">4</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Week 3 — Connect CI/CD Pipeline</h3>
        <p>Integrate your test suite with Jenkins or GitHub Actions so AI tests run automatically on every code push. Set up Slack alerts for failures.</p>
        <div class="code-block">
<span class="comment"># GitHub Actions — .github/workflows/ai-tests.yml</span>
<span class="kw">name</span>: AI-Powered Test Suite
<span class="kw">on</span>: [push, pull_request]
<span class="kw">jobs</span>:
  test:
    <span class="kw">runs-on</span>: ubuntu-latest
    <span class="kw">steps</span>:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - <span class="kw">name</span>: Run Selenium + Healenium Tests
        <span class="kw">run</span>: mvn test -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false
      - <span class="kw">name</span>: Generate Allure Report
        <span class="kw">run</span>: mvn allure:report
      - <span class="kw">name</span>: Notify Slack on Failure
        <span class="kw">if</span>: failure()
        uses: slackapi/slack-github-action@v1
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
      <div class="step-num">5</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3>Week 4 — Team Training & Prompt Library</h3>
        <p>Run a half-day workshop with the QA team. Build a shared prompt library in Confluence. Establish AI review checkpoints in your test process.</p>
        <div class="code-block">
<span class="comment">## TRAINING AGENDA (4 hours):</span>
Hour 1: AI tool overview + live demo (Testsigma + Claude)
Hour 2: Hands-on: Generate test cases from real sprint stories
Hour 3: Selenium + Healenium: Add self-healing to existing suite
Hour 4: Defect analysis with AI — paste logs, get root cause

<span class="comment">## CONFLUENCE PAGE STRUCTURE:</span>
QA AI Toolkit/
├── Prompt Templates (30+ tested prompts)
├── Tool Credentials & Access
├── Best Practices & Guardrails
└── Sprint AI Test Review Checklist
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

